    "javaABI": "BaseSource.login(): void. Same retained nullable String getLoginJs(), Java MutableMap<String,String> result, exact existing BookSource/RuleEnvironment/RuntimeTask/Rhino.",
    "sequence": [
      "The locked BaseSource.login trims/unwraps getLoginJs, skips blank, appends mandatory login.apply(this) or throws, ignores completion. Production preserves the method body after owner-open/diagnostic-protection guards.",
      "The locked SourceLoginDialog confirmation reads form data, removes raw loginInfo and does not execute JS for an empty map; a known false put stops before login JS; accepted nonempty credentials are stored before optional login JS executes.",
      "The real dialog passes java=SourceLoginJsExtensions, result=a Java form Map, actual viewModel book/chapter and isLongClick=false. This standalone form has no Book/Chapter context, so passes null as the actual context.",
      "JS completion is ignored. Credentials remain accepted if later JS/HTTP fails; loginHeader/Cookies change only through explicit original source/HTTP owner writes. Never interpret returned JSON as a header.",
      "The Android dialog has lifecycle cancellation but no fixed thirty-second form timer. Thirty seconds in this slice is the finite native embedding deadline, including the same source-lock wait."
    ],
    "finiteJavaHost": "OriginalSourceLoginHost borrows the same original source/environment/task, existing AnalyzeRule and existing HTTP. getSource/getTag/get/put, ajax and parsing delegates are connected. Browser/UI refresh/clipboard/toast capabilities throw typed unsupported. No Book or Chapter is fabricated."
  },
  "production": [
    "Product doLogin confirmation now calls the existing BookSourceFetcher.mainJSService.originalFormLogin for traditional text sources. The same source actor acquires its existing source lock, accepts the actual source revision and calls the same NativeLegadoOriginalPreviewExecutor/LegadoRuntimeProcess with no Book grant.",
    "Package public formLoginOriginal encodes the bounded request and uses existing executeOriginal worker/task/deadline/cancellation/effect receipt mechanisms. Runtime dispatch runs the same original JVM/Rhino/source owner, never JSC as a fallback.",
    "Existing AnalyzeByJSonPath.onError and optional NetworkUtils diagnostic callbacks now delegate to the same platform/task; default non-sensitive FINE logger/Throwable diagnostics and the existing two-argument URL Java ABI remain. Sensitive login tasks suppress those raw diagnostics without a new parser, global log filter or thread-local owner.",
    "Submitted secret text remains on the existing dedicated source.login-info/LoginManager Keychain owner. Explicit loginHeader remains on the already connected existing LoginManager/header/Cookie owner. No new credential store, generic-cache secret mirror, engine or HTTP client is added.",
    "A task metadata flag suppresses authored log payloads and sanitizes arbitrary exceptions for formLogin. The same protection is activated before direct BaseSource.login, so callback-driven login does not expose returned script/HTTP/credential descriptions. Swift service/UI report only static error code and effect count.",
    "The traditional caller merges its complete existing values snapshot with only visible text/password edits, preserves hidden keys and explicit empty edits, and skips the legacy mandatory-field gate. Synthesis/classification run off main with no new Keychain read. MainJs/media retain their old validation/route. The owned SwiftUI submission Task is cancelled on disappearance; cancellation suppresses late alerts. The existing native controls, form, localization and previews remain. Nontraditional mainJs/media, dynamic loginUi loading and menu button flows retain their prior route, outside this slice.",
    "Eight existing exact portedSources byte/hash rows are updated and one new finite-host row/runtime class is added. All other original archive/provenance/license/resource/acceptance fields remain byte-equivalent in the manifest data."
  ],
